  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A number is called a palindrome if it reads the same backward as well as forward. For example <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>285582</mn></math> is a six digit palindrome. The number of six digit palindromes, which are divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>,</mo></math> is ________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d902ff78-af96-41d8-9b3e-7c9aaaed4e36-image-alt.png\" style=\"width: 256px; height: 66px;\" /></p><p>Palindrome Numbers only in this form will be divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn></math>.</p><p>Numbers can be&nbsp; between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Number of ways of&nbsp;selecting value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>Similarly&nbsp; number of ways of choosing value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp; (As a and b can also be same)</p><p>Therefore, Total number of ways of getting palindrome numbers divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
